Licence for derived data in this archive
=======================================

The MIT licence in LICENSE covers the source code. It does not cover data.

Derived data, when a version of this archive carries it, is released under
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

"Derived data" means aggregates computed by the code in this archive: age-by-age
co-arrival matrices, the age-specific coverage profile, the measured per-cell
masking fill, the administrative-dong crosswalk, and the calendar and policy
panel.

WHAT IS NOT COVERED, AND IS NOT HERE
------------------------------------

The Seoul Living Migration (생활이동) administrative-dong product itself is NOT
redistributed in this archive, in any form, at any resolution. It is published
by the Seoul Metropolitan Government through the Seoul Open Data Plaza under its
own terms, which permit free use on attribution. Retrieve it with the download
helpers under eda/ and verify it against the stored SHA-256 manifest.

The Korean nationwide contact survey is not redistributed either. It is
available from its own public release (doi:10.1038/s41597-026-06896-y) under its
own licence and its own ethical approval.

Resident registration, registered-foreigner and SGIS covariate files come from
행정안전부, 법무부 and SGIS respectively. They are NOT covered by the Seoul
terms and each carries its own conditions.

ATTRIBUTION
-----------

Reuse of any derived aggregate must credit both this deposit and the upstream
Seoul Metropolitan Government release it was computed from. Attribution to this
deposit alone is not sufficient.

RE-IDENTIFICATION
-----------------

The source product already suppresses cells below three at publication. What is
released here is aggregation at the matrix level, coarser than the source cells,
so it adds no re-identification risk beyond the published product.
